<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/parties">Parties</a> lists the parties booked at your location, grouped by day. Each card shows the
        birthday child, the times, the party type, how many are coming, the room, the food, the host and any allergies, with a
        payment badge in the corner. Click a card to open the party.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Finding a party">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Upcoming</strong> and <strong>Past</strong> switch between parties still to come and ones that have happened.</li>
            <li><strong>Payment</strong> narrows the list to unpaid, deposit paid or paid in full parties.</li>
            <li>Tick <strong>Show cancelled</strong> to include cancelled parties as well.</li>
            <li>Admins get a <strong>Location</strong> picker. Managers see the parties at the location they signed in to.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Booking a party">
        <ol>
            <li>Press <strong>Book a party</strong>.</li>
            <li>Enter the birthday child's <strong>Name</strong> and the age they're <strong>Turning</strong>.</li>
            <li>Pick the <strong>Date</strong> and the <strong>Arrival</strong> time. The <strong>Finish</strong>, <strong>Eating time</strong>
                and <strong>Laser tag time</strong> fill in from the arrival time using the location's
                <a href="/manage/parties/settings">Party Settings</a>. Change any of them and Lanyard leaves that one alone.</li>
            <li>Add the <strong>Party type</strong>. Types you've used before appear as buttons underneath, so one click fills it in.</li>
            <li>Fill in the <strong>Room or table</strong>, choose <strong>Hot food</strong> or <strong>Cold food</strong>, and pick the
                <strong>Party host</strong> from the staff at the location.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>Contact</strong>, enter the parent or guardian's name and phone number, and their email if you have it.</li>
            <li>Enter how many <strong>Children coming</strong> and <strong>Adults</strong>, plus any allergies or dietary needs and other notes.</li>
            <li>Enter the <strong>Total price</strong> and <strong>Deposit</strong> if you know them, then press <strong>Book party</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            To change a party later, open it, edit the details and press <strong>Save changes</strong>. On an existing party the
            times no longer fill themselves in.
        </FluentText>
        <HelpNote>
            The child's name, the parent's name and phone, and at least one child coming are required. The party has to finish
            after it starts, and the eating and laser tag times have to fall within it.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
    <HelpSection Title="Private hire">
        <FluentText>
            To book the venue for a private hire instead of a kids' party, select <strong>Private hire</strong> under
            <strong>Booking</strong> on Book a Party, then choose what it's for under <strong>Hire for</strong>:
            <strong>Play only</strong>, <strong>Laser tag + Play</strong> or <strong>Laser tag only</strong>.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            A hire only needs who booked it, the date and times, how many guests are coming, notes and payment. The birthday
            child, food, party type and printouts aren't used. Hires show on the Parties list as "Private hire" with the name of
            the person who booked.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            Set the extra staff each kind of hire needs under <strong>Party staffing</strong> on Party Settings.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
